1
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:05,504
Literate is a free, open-source extension
built to read to you.

2
00:00:05,929 --> 00:00:10,136
It works with articles, selected text, and
local PDFs.

3
00:00:10,136 --> 00:00:13,636
Instant voice mode uses voices already
installed on your device

4
00:00:13,636 --> 00:00:17,521
and can start almost immediately, even on
slower devices,

5
00:00:17,816 --> 00:00:21,576
though some voices may sound robotic.
Natural voice mode

6
00:00:21,576 --> 00:00:25,656
uses a downloaded Kokoro model for more
natural narration, but may need

7
00:00:25,656 --> 00:00:29,980
time to warm up before playback. Its files
stay cached for later reading.

8
00:00:31,282 --> 00:00:35,676
On an article, you can listen to the main
text with words highlighted as it plays.

9
00:00:35,676 --> 00:00:41,041
Selected passages also have a right-click
option: Read selection aloud.

10
00:00:41,536 --> 00:00:45,181
The section picker lets you focus on a
particular part of the page,

11
00:00:45,516 --> 00:00:49,081
leaving sidebars and related stories
outside the reading area.

12
00:00:49,496 --> 00:00:53,716
The mini player keeps scrolling text
nearby. You can click individual

13
00:00:53,716 --> 00:00:58,401
words to jump around, or pin the player
above other windows in supported browsers.

14
00:00:59,016 --> 00:01:03,156
You can customize the narration speed and
the extension’s appearance, with

15
00:01:03,156 --> 00:01:08,621
light and dark modes and a choice of
accent colors. Periwinkle is the default.

16
00:01:09,136 --> 00:01:14,176
Local PDFs are supported with Chrome’s
file-access permission. The reader works

17
00:01:14,176 --> 00:01:18,661
with existing text, while scanned
documents need text recognition first.

18
00:01:19,136 --> 00:01:24,221
The speech runs on your device. Kokoro’s
files download from Hugging Face,

19
00:01:24,256 --> 00:01:28,381
and the source page needs to remain open
while the mini player is in use.
